---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout locale="en">
  <main class="policy">
    <section class="policy-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>beisammen</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This page describes the data categories currently used by the beisammen
        app and website. It is intended as product-facing documentation and
        should be reviewed with counsel before a broad public release.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: April 18, 2026</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who this applies to</h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to the beisammen mobile app, the beisammen website,
        and the hosted backend services used to operate them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Data we process</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you use the product, we may process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>account and sign-in data needed for authentication via WorkOS</li>
        <li>profile data such as your display name, email address, and profile image</li>
        <li>circle, invite, and membership data used to manage private groups</li>
        <li>media metadata such as filenames, mime types, timestamps, and upload state</li>
        <li>media files you choose to upload, stored on the configured S3-compatible storage</li>
        <li>optional location data derived from embedded photo metadata or device permission flows</li>
        <li>waitlist form submissions you send through the website</li>
        <li>basic technical logs needed to operate, secure, and debug the service</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How we use this data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>to authenticate users and keep sessions active</li>
        <li>to create and operate private circles, invites, and shared libraries</li>
        <li>to upload, process, and display shared photos and videos</li>
        <li>to attach optional place labels to media when location information is available</li>
        <li>to respond to waitlist requests and product access inquiries</li>
        <li>to maintain security, prevent abuse, and troubleshoot service problems</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <p>The mobile app may request access to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>photos and videos, to select and save media</li>
        <li>camera, to capture photos and videos</li>
        <li>microphone, to record video with audio</li>
        <li>location, to enrich media with place information when you allow it</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These permissions support core sharing features. You can deny optional
        permissions, but some features may no longer work as intended.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Storage and processors</h2>
      <p>
        beisammen uses Convex as its application backend and WorkOS for
        authentication. Original media files are designed to live on
        S3-compatible storage configured for the active deployment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain account, group, and media records for as long as they are
        needed to operate the service or until they are deleted from the active
        deployment. Retention details may differ for self-hosted deployments.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>you can choose whether to upload media</li>
        <li>you can choose whether to grant optional device permissions</li>
        <li>you can leave the waitlist by contacting the operator of the deployment</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy inquiries related to the official beisammen deployment, use
        the contact details published on <a href="https://beisammen.app/en/">beisammen.app</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy {
    width: min(52rem, calc(100vw - 2rem));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 0 6rem;
    color: #f1e7d2;
  }
  .policy-hero {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .eyebrow,
  .meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgba(241, 231, 210, 0.64);
  }
  h1,
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 4.8rem);
    line-height: 0.94;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 1rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.2rem);
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
  }
  section + section {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  p,
  li {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: rgba(241, 231, 210, 0.84);
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 42rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }
  a {
    color: #f4a261;
  }
</style>
